rac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}-xy)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}-xy)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}-xy)\\,k \\\\  & =(4x-y)\\text{ }i-x\\text{ }j+2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(-2,-3,1) & =(4(-2)-(-3))\\,i-(-2)\\,j+2(1)\\,k \\\\  & =-5\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-5\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(-2,-3,1).$" 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406818 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406816 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406818 1069 "q-130719" 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406818 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406818 1071 "Consider the plane curve $2y-x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y}).$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(2,1).$" 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406818 1072 #uuid "ef115c0b-3981-5c8f-8e9d-f41c20799c2d" 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406818 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y-x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y})-2y+x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y})-2y+x,$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(2,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(2,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y})-2y+x)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y})-2y+x)j \\\\  & =(\\frac{2y}{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2y}+1)i+(\\frac{2y}{x}\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{2{y}^{2}})-2)j \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{x}+1)i+(-\\frac{1}{y}-2)j \\\\ ∇f(2,1) & =(\\frac{1}{2}+1)i+(-\\frac{1}{1}-2)j \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\,i-3\\,j \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2},-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(3,1)=⟨\\frac{3}{2},-3⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(2,1).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-2}{(\\frac{3}{2})} & =\\frac{y-1}{(-3)} \\\\ -3(x-2) & =\\frac{3}{2}(y-1) \\\\ -6(x-2) & =3(y-1) \\\\ -2(x-2) & =y-1 \\\\ -2x+4 & =y-1 \\\\ 2x+y-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406819 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406820 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406819 1062 #uuid "6c546df4-95bc-53a6-8314-f63e977926a5" 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406819 1063 #edb/ref 17592186406817 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406820 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406821 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406820 1062 #uuid "854e10c9-a2d4-5612-8167-ef459f663827" 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406820 1063 #edb/ref 17592186406818 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406821 1062 #uuid "9536b8a9-959c-5b6e-8ff0-53d077d7ad52" 13194139533517 17592186045585 true] [17592186406821 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265967 13194139533517 17592186045585 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-70dc8b50-8f87-5b55-9f2e-265dbd1adbfc" 17592186406804 "answer-1a1d5e01-e81c-5544-a929-055747dc7f77" 17592186406805 "answer-1dd5310c-dfc2-5a7d-bac5-5825f5064da6" 17592186406806 "answer-4bd3692c-18d7-5dde-9e79-ca2c71d664a2" 17592186406807 "answer-82778c6a-7758-50ec-ad08-3720a9d490ae" 17592186406808 "answer-cd07008c-2d5e-5372-aa7f-53d2714271f3" 17592186406809 "answer-cdae5c41-27fa-5c55-9f46-cceeabd59a1a" 17592186406810 "answer-dbcc8cce-7237-5eb6-ac41-6a5901ea8c81" 17592186406811 "answer-e415ebda-6949-5999-a629-48685dbda1c0" 17592186406812 "answer-e8a7f1a1-3119-55e9-ab80-51ececd277a7" 17592186406813 "answer-ecf6508f-66f3-52c3-8fbf-477ac88383db" 17592186406814 "answer-field-4f78fc66-8357-5b97-ab1a-5d79ee0e7c85" 17592186406815 "answer-field-f9e7ba4e-7d61-5628-8ce5-894dfba410f8" 17592186406816 "question-07